PasspointManager: Ask for ANQP data only with a Passpoint profile saved

Android asks every Hotspot 2.0 network it sees for ANQP data after a scan,
even with no Passpoint profile to match it against. The query takes the
radio off its channel while connected, and the mt76x8 driver on the Echo
Shows then loses most traffic until Wi-Fi reconnects. Without a profile
nothing uses the answer, so skip the query.

diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/hotspot2/PasspointManager.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/hotspot2/PasspointManager.java
index ad66f11..51d9a86 100644
--- a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/hotspot2/PasspointManager.java
+++ b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/hotspot2/PasspointManager.java
@@ -851,7 +851,11 @@ public class PasspointManager {
                 vsa.anqpDomainID);
         ANQPData anqpEntry = mAnqpCache.getEntry(anqpKey);
         if (anqpEntry == null) {
-            if (anqpRequestAllowed) {
+            // Kiosk Satellite Edition: ask only when a Passpoint profile can use the answer. The
+            // query takes the radio off its channel, and the Echo Shows' Wi-Fi driver then loses
+            // most traffic until Wi-Fi reconnects, so one nearby Hotspot 2.0 network was enough
+            // to break the connection.
+            if (anqpRequestAllowed && !mProviders.isEmpty()) {
                 mAnqpRequestManager.requestANQPElements(bssid, anqpKey,
                         roamingConsortium.anqpOICount > 0, vsa.hsRelease);
             }
